BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mister Rogers Free Day
DTSTART:20260320T100000
DTEND:20260320T170000
UID:75ebc618bba7de80@shumway-family-events
DESCRIPTION:Fred Rogers is a beloved icon for Pittsburgh and we believe it
 ’s important to continue to memorialize his wonderful and meaningful wor
 k\, as well as help today’s children and families better relate to his m
 any messages of kindness\, acceptance and individuality. \nWe celebrate th
 e life and work of Fred Rogers on his birthday with Free Admission to the 
 Children’s Museum. \nYou can find these iconic items from Mister Rogers
 ’ Neighborhood in the Children’s Museum: \nOriginal Puppets from Miste
 r Rogers’ Neighborhood\nLocated in the Nursery\nKing Friday XIII\, Queen
  Sara Saturday\, Henrietta Pussycat\, X the Owl\, Lady Elaine Fairchilde\,
  Daniel Striped Tiger and Gran Pere greet you as you enter the Nursery spa
 ce. \nMister Rogers’ Sweater\nLocated in The Kindness Gallery\nDid you k
 now that Fred Rogers’ mother knitted him the iconic sweater that he chan
 ged into each episode? See one of Fred’s sweaters on display above a rec
 ord player where you can play Daniel Tiger’s Strategy Songs \nFred Roger
 s & Children’s Museum of Pittsburgh\nFred Rogers has been very important
  for Children’s Museum of Pittsburgh – as an advisor\, a mentor and a 
 friend. Here’s a chronology of the work we’ve done with him and his te
 am through years: \nIn 1998\, the Children’s Museum\, along with Fred Ro
 gers and his company Family Communications\, Inc. (FCI)\, created Mister R
 ogers’ Neighborhood: A Hands-on Exhibit. The exhibit welcomed hundreds o
 f thousands of visitors for almost 10 years – both children who loved th
 e imaginative set pieces and adults who recalled their love of the televis
 ion show as children.  A sister exhibit traveled to other museums across 
 the country for more than eight years\, making friends and good neighbors 
 for Pittsburgh wherever it went.  At the end of its tour\, in the spirit 
 of Mister Rogers\, the traveling exhibit was given to the Louisiana Childr
 en’s Museum\, whose facility had been devastated by Hurricane Katrina in
  2005. \nIn 2007\, we created the How People Make Things exhibit in collab
 oration with FCI to tell the story of how everyday items are manufactured\
 , inspired by the factory tour segments from the “Mister Rogers’ Neigh
 borhood” television series.  This exhibit continues to tour to museums 
 across the country. \nIn October 2011\, the Museum refurbished many of the
  exhibit components from the Neighborhood and integrated them throughout a
 ll three floors of the Children’s Museum. \nIn August 2015\, King Friday
 ’s Castle and Mister Rogers’ Neighborhood Trolley\, both of which were
  showing wear from the attention of many children over the years\, were ta
 ken down. \nIn June 2016\, we opened a new exhibit on Daniel Tiger’s Nei
 ghborhood: A Grr-ific Exhibit in partnership with The Fred Rogers Company
 \, based on Daniel Tiger’s Neighborhood\, the first TV series inspired b
 y the original Mister Rogers’ Neighborhood series.  By bringing the wor
 ld and characters of this award-winning animated series to life in an inte
 ractive exhibit\, the important messages of Fred Rogers continue to be exp
 ressed to children and families in fun\, imaginative ways. \nIn 2019\, the
  Museum worked with our partners at Fred Rogers Productions (FRP\, formerl
 y Family Communications\, Inc.) to create a mini version of the exhibition
  Daniel Tiger’s Neighborhood : A Grr-ffic Exhibit at Kidsport at the Pit
 tsburgh International Airport. \nIn 2021\, we partnered with FRP again to 
 develop a pop-up exhibit about the television series Donkey Hodie\,  an i
 maginative puppet series that debuted in 2021. The series features the gra
 nddaughter of the Donkey Hodie character from the original Mister Rogers
 ’ Neighborhood show\, now reimagined as “Grampy Hodie”.\n\n⏰ PRO T
 IP: Free admission on Mister Rogers' birthday (March 20) – arrive at ope
 ning to avoid crowds.\n👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 Cousin Friendly (ages 8-1
 2)\n\nSource: Children's Museum of Pittsburgh\n🔗 https://secure.pittsbu
 rghkids.org/admission/1488#new_tab
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Coming up: Mister Rogers Free Day
TRIGGER:-P6DT15H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
